@@@ file: README.md kind=web lang=ts @@@
# End-to-end tests (Playwright)

Scaffolded by {{generated_by}}.

| Task | Command (from `{{out}}/`) |
|---|---|
| Install | `npm ci` (first time: `npm install`, commit `package-lock.json`), then `npx playwright install --with-deps` |
| Run everything | `npx playwright test` |
| Smoke subset | `npx playwright test --grep @smoke` |
| One browser | `npx playwright test --project=chromium` |
| Debug a failure | `npx playwright show-report` (traces are kept for failed tests) |

- `E2E_BASE_URL` selects the app under test (default `{{base_url}}`); without it the configured
  `webServer` starts the app.
- `E2E_USERNAME` / `E2E_PASSWORD` enable the per-worker login in `fixtures.ts`.
- Locators: `getByRole` and `getByLabel` first, then `getByTestId` (`data-testid`); never CSS
  structure or XPath. Waits: web-first assertions, never `waitForTimeout`.
- Determinism: `page.clock` for time, `page.route` / `page.routeFromHAR` for third-party calls.
- CI (`.github/workflows/e2e-web.yml`): 4 shards, retries only in CI with `failOnFlakyTests`,
  blob reports merged into one HTML report and `junit.xml`.

@@@ file: .github/workflows/e2e-web.yml kind=web lang=ts scope=repo @@@
{{header}}
# Playwright end-to-end tests in 4 shards; the report job merges the blob reports into one HTML
# report and one JUnit file. Edit freely: a later `verify` reports weakening edits as findings.
name: e2e-web

on:
  pull_request:
  push:
    branches: [{{default_branch}}]
  workflow_dispatch:

permissions:
  contents: read

concurrency:
  group: e2e-web-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

jobs:
  test:
    name: e2e (shard ${{ matrix.shardIndex }}/${{ matrix.shardTotal }})
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 60
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        shardIndex: [1, 2, 3, 4]
        shardTotal: [4]
    defaults:
      run:
        shell: bash
        working-directory: {{out}}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v7
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7
        with:
          node-version: 24
          cache: npm
          cache-dependency-path: {{out}}/package-lock.json
{{app_install}}
      - name: Install the e2e project
        run: npm ci
      - name: Install browsers (not cached, as Playwright recommends)
        run: npx playwright install --with-deps
      - name: Run the shard
        run: npx playwright test --shard=${{ matrix.shardIndex }}/${{ matrix.shardTotal }}
        env:
          E2E_BASE_URL: ${{ vars.E2E_BASE_URL }}
          E2E_USERNAME: ${{ vars.E2E_USERNAME }}
          E2E_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.E2E_PASSWORD }}
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7
        if: ${{ !cancelled() }}
        with:
          name: blob-report-${{ matrix.shardIndex }}
          path: {{out}}/blob-report
          retention-days: 1

  report:
    name: e2e report
    if: ${{ !cancelled() }}
    needs: [test]
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    defaults:
      run:
        shell: bash
        working-directory: {{out}}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v7
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7
        with:
          node-version: 24
          cache: npm
          cache-dependency-path: {{out}}/package-lock.json
      - run: npm ci
      - uses: actions/download-artifact@v8
        with:
          path: {{out}}/all-blob-reports
          pattern: blob-report-*
          merge-multiple: true
      - name: Merge the shard reports into HTML and JUnit
        run: npx playwright merge-reports --reporter html,junit ./all-blob-reports
        env:
          PLAYWRIGHT_JUNIT_OUTPUT_NAME: junit.xml
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7
        with:
          name: playwright-report
          path: |
            {{out}}/playwright-report
            {{out}}/junit.xml
          retention-days: 14

